  "details": "Idk what it is but when there is a lobby with more than 10 people in a world, whenever I start loading avatars around me, My VRChat freezes, and I try to recover it by putting my quest pro into sleep mode, and then turning it back on again to try to get back into VR, because it seems my entire PC locks up when avatars are trying to fully load.\n\nAfter it says \"UH OH Steam has encountered an error and must restart (Error -203)\"\n\nIdk what it is. I tried clean installing VRChat, SteamVR, Doing the script registery edits that cleans out VRChat settings. Uninstalling ALL addons such as OVR Toolkit & XSOverlay (only one I can't remove is Virtual Desktop & Open-Spacecalibrator).\n\nThis started happening recently.\n\nIdk what to do but I literally cannot play anymore because I keep crashing when people are loading around me.\n\nI even set the settings to only load 10 meters around me, and only 5 avatars at a time. Still crash.\n\nHardware:\n\nI5-11400F\n\n32 GB DDR4 Ram (I think 3200)\n\nWindows 11\n\nRTX 4060\n\nUsing Quest Pro with Virtual Desktop",
